{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35562-wraith20-all-the-arcanoi-please","id":35562,"title":"Wraith20: All the Arcanoi, Please.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T07:26:40-08:00","id":35562,"title":"Wraith20: All the Arcanoi, Please.","content":"With the new 30% off sale on all Wraith material, I figured I could just grab the non-Western Arcanoi pretty easily. Except, no, I can't. They're scattered around in three different books. Even though the Player's Guide is supposed to have information on the non-Stygian kingdoms of the dead, I have to get The Great War for the African and Indian signature Arcanoi. I have to get the Shadow Player's Guide for the Caribbean Arcanoi. Whaat?<br /> <br /> It kinda makes sense that the Jade Arcanoi are in the China book, at least. I understand the Risen Arcanoi and the Dark Arcanoi being in books about Risen and Specters, respectively. Totally sensible.<br /> <br /> It'd be super awesome if Wraith 20 combines the Arcanoi together. All of them. Admittedly, V20 didn't have to fit in 35 different powers (there's 35 Arcanoi total), but Disciplines go up to 9, so there's less powers in total. Especially considering Necromancy, Thaumaturgy, Koldunic Sorcery, etc. Please? I'll give you cookies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T08:26:54-08:00","id":35586,"title":"","content":"Yeah like I said in another thread I would love to have the foreign Arcanoi in the Wr20 book but I can understand just sticking with the Stygian ones along with all their variants would be fine and instead having a supplement with details on all the other Dark Kingdoms along with their Arcanoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:13:45-08:00","id":35802,"title":"","content":"I'll chime in with a hope that <b>Wr20</b> shall have those alternate powers, such as the ones for the Arcanos Inhabit that had anything to do with items that existed before the transistor-age... Which I thought to find in <i>Guildbook: Artificers</i> and did not. I only found out <i>long</i> after the line ended that the powers I sought were called Kinesis and could be found in <i>Wraith: the Great War</i>.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I'm all for even the 'Stygian Arcanoi' all appearing in <b>Wr20</b>, but seriously? I already KNOW that I'm gonna spend a lot on this project, regardless of what's in there or not in there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:19:33-08:00","id":35838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Telgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/35562-wraith20-all-the-arcanoi-please#post35562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It'd be super awesome if Wraith 20 combines the Arcanoi together. All of them. Admittedly, V20 didn't have to fit in 35 different powers (there's 35 Arcanoi total), but Disciplines go up to 9, so there's less powers in total. Especially considering Necromancy, Thaumaturgy, Koldunic Sorcery, etc. Please? I'll give you cookies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be shocked if all the various Arcanoi didn't get included. V20 has 32 Disciplines in it (though that's with 3 sorcery ones), four of which are have multiple paths. If you counted each Thaum/Sorcery/Necro path as a separate Discipline that would easily blow way past the 35 Arcanoi in terms of numbers.<br /> <br /> I can see maybe a few of them getting left out. Like say the Risen one if Wr20 is going to get a separate Risen book. But if V20 could get all that in there, Wr20 should be able to get all the Arcanoi in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:48:22-08:00","id":35861,"title":"","content":"Also would the opportunity to expand the secrets of the guilds and Styx on Arcanoi. Apart from the Add Arcanoi Obsidian (which he missed).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:22:34-08:00","id":36139,"title":"","content":"I'd prefer to have all the Stygian Arcanoi in the core Wr20, and then a Dark Kingdoms/Far Shores tome with everything else. Vampire may have more Disciplines wordcount overall, but (hopefully) Shadowguiding and alternate Shadowguiding methods will take up a large chunk of text.<br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:26:13-08:00","id":36144,"title":"","content":"Eh... they can fit that stuff into the parts where Vampire has the Roads and Paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}